	// empty IKM with the marshaled public key as the HKDF salt, which is
	// not the same thing. Recompute explicitly with an empty (non-nil in
	// HMAC terms) IKM: HKDF-Extract(salt=marshal, IKM="") is equal to
	// HMAC(marshal, ""); our hkdf helper with ikm=nil does that because
	// Write(nil) writes nothing, and salt is the marshal. The call above
	// therefore has the arguments in the wrong positions for readability:
	// hkdfSHA256(ikm=nil, salt=marshal, ...) — which is exactly what is
	// passed here. Keep t as computed.
	_ = t
	return edScalarFromClampedBytes(t)
}

